#### a plain scalar formula origin (=1+1) still contributes 2 to SUM

- Verify: a plain scalar formula origin (=1+1) still contributes 2 to SUM
   - Expected: _disp(sh, "G1") equals `9`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 10 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
step("Verify: a plain scalar formula origin (=1+1) still contributes 2 to SUM")
var sh = Sheet.new("f")
sh.set_value("A1", "3")
sh.set_value("B1", "4")
sh.set_value("C1", "=1+1")
sh = recalculate_formula_cells(sh)
sh.set_value("G1", "=SUM(A1:C1)")
sh = recalculate_formula_cells(sh)
expect(_disp(sh, "G1")).to_equal("9")
```

